--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,18 @@ import { resolvePointer } from 'json-toolkit';
 
 resolvePointer({ foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }, '/foo/0'); // => 'bar'
 ```
+
+### JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies a [JSON Patch](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902) — an
+array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` or `test` operations — to a JSON document and
+returns the resulting document as a new value, leaving `document` and `patch` untouched. It throws a
+`JsonPatchError` when the patch is not syntactically valid, or when one of its operations fails (for
+example, a path that does not resolve, or a failed `test`).
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+applyPatch({ foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }, [{ op: 'add', path: '/foo/1', value: 'qux' }]);
+// => { foo: ['bar', 'qux', 'baz'] }
+```
